Subject: Result of investigation on circle gate malfunction on 25 October

Dear IBM Team,

This is [your name] from the Omiya Data Center Operations team.

Regarding the circle gate passage issue that occurred on 25 October, we have completed our investigation together with the equipment vendor. Please find the summary of the results below.
	1.	Condition of the equipment

	•	A detailed inspection by the manufacturer on 18 November confirmed that there is no abnormality in the circle gate hardware or control system.

	2.	Investigation results

	•	The “one-person check” inside the gate is performed using several sensors: a transmissive sensor, a mat switch and a weight sensor.
	•	According to the manufacturer, it is highly likely that the card-reader part of the gate passed through the transmissive sensor and was therefore mis-detected as “two persons entering”.
	•	As the transmissive sensor is an optical type, the colour of clothing (including black clothes or gloves) does not affect the detection.
	•	During on-site simulations, we confirmed that if a person stands with their feet slightly apart on the mat and shifts their weight from side to side, the weight sensor may not detect the person correctly, which can cause an error and prevent smooth passage.
	•	The sensors are installed at approximately 30 cm and 80 cm from the floor, so the body needs to be close enough to the card reader / back side of the gate to be detected reliably.

	3.	Preventive actions

	•	We will prepare and share usage instructions for the circle gate, including guidance such as:
	•	When entering, stand with both heels on the inner line marked on the floor.
	•	Avoid standing too far away from the card reader or leaning back while the one-person check is being performed.
	•	Avoid excessive body movement or shifting weight from side to side until the gate has completed the check.
	•	Internally, this case is being handled under our “Problem Management” process rather than as an incident, and we will continue to monitor the situation.

We hope this explanation clarifies the cause of the event and our preventive measures.
